1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,561
Now listen carefully.

2
00:00:01,561 --> 00:00:06,140
This may be the single most important rule in Indian health insurance.

3
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:08,697
It is called the moratorium period.

4
00:00:08,697 --> 00:00:11,179
Earlier, this period was eight years.

5
00:00:11,179 --> 00:00:17,085
But in twenty twenty-four, the I-R-D-A-I brought it down from eight years to five years.

6
00:00:17,085 --> 00:00:22,113
That means sixty continuous months in a row, with no break in your policy.

7
00:00:22,113 --> 00:00:23,942
So, what does it mean for you?

8
00:00:25,036 --> 00:00:36,251
After five years of continuous cover, the insurance company legally CANNOT question your policy or your claim on grounds of non-disclosure, like an old disease you did not mention.

9
00:00:36,251 --> 00:00:37,339
Read that again.

10
00:00:37,339 --> 00:00:42,276
After five years, an old health history cannot be used as an excuse.

11
00:00:42,276 --> 00:00:44,592
There is only one single exception.

12
00:00:44,592 --> 00:00:47,852
Proven fraud that the company has to establish.

13
00:00:47,852 --> 00:00:53,809
Not a forgotten fever, not an undiagnosed ache... active, deliberate fraud.

14
00:00:53,809 --> 00:01:00,960
Your normal policy limits and exclusions still apply, and if you port your policy to another insurer, your years move with you.

15
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:04,778
If you cancel and buy a new one, the count resets to zero.

16
00:01:04,778 --> 00:01:07,359
Now think about our family at the billing counter.

17
00:01:07,359 --> 00:01:09,731
Six years of continuous policy.

18
00:01:09,731 --> 00:01:12,103
A letter that says non-disclosure.

19
00:01:12,103 --> 00:01:15,971
That excuse directly violates the I-R-D-A-I rule.

20
00:01:15,971 --> 00:01:18,837
And there is one more rule... a clock.

21
00:01:18,837 --> 00:01:26,586
When the hospital sends the final discharge request to the insurance company, the company must give final approval within three hours.

22
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:30,607
I-R-D-A-I mandates that the patient should not be made to wait.

23
00:01:30,607 --> 00:01:40,552
If the approval comes later than three hours, any extra amount the hospital charges for that delay is paid by the insurance company from its own funds... not by you.

24
00:01:40,552 --> 00:01:43,811
Remember this rule, and ask for it at the discharge counter.

